      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Origin and Evolution of the Atmosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Nitrogen (78.08%) and Oxygen (20.95%) comprise nearly 99% of the dry atmosphere by volume.",
        "The troposphere contains almost all atmospheric water vapor and aerosols, hosting all weather phenomena.",
        "Temperature in the troposphere decreases with altitude at the normal lapse rate of 6.5°C per 1,000 meters.",
        "The stratosphere contains the ozone layer which protects the Earth by absorbing harmful ultraviolet radiation.",
        "Atmospheric density and pressure decrease rapidly and exponentially with increasing altitude."
      ],
      "id": "jyzhm6g"
