    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Troposphere height is greatest at the equator (~18 km) due to strong convection currents and lowest at the poles (~8 km).",
        "The stratosphere is free from clouds and turbulent weather, making it the ideal layer for flying jet aircraft.",
        "The ionosphere, located within the thermosphere, contains charged particles that reflect radio waves back to Earth.",
        "Ozone concentration is measured in Dobson Units (DU), and its depletion is heavily targeted in competitive exams."
